# Whole-sky three-basis comparison

Created `/Game/RXSkySystem/Cubeless/Maps/L_RXSkySystem_ThreeBasis` from the current saved `L_RXSkySystem_Cubeless`. The original preview, original BP and six-direction cloud materials remain available. The new level uses `Cubeless/ThreeBasis/BP_RXSkySystem_ThreeBasis` and its own cloud material/instance. All 115 instance-editable source BP properties were copied and compared equal before removing the copied old sky actor. Dome transforms/visibility, other actors and the original GameMode were preserved. The existing individual test card is still a separate comparison object; it was not rebaked as part of the dome.

## Bake

- Source: frozen `Baking/Cubeless/Layouts/Study03_Hybrid_20260920/Materials/MI_CloudSource`, the source of the active whole-sky bake, including the tiled background.
- New package: `Baking/Bakes/Cubeless_Beauty45_20260920`.
- Output: `T_Cubeless_Beauty45_20260920_Beauty45_RGBA`, 4096 square linear HDR RGBA.
- R: +45 degree light elevation, azimuth 0; G: -45 degree elevation, azimuth 0; B: elevation 0, azimuth 180; A: original coverage.
- One global light per pass across all cube faces avoids lighting discontinuities at face seams. This is a fixed world-space basis, not a per-cloud/view-dependent beauty light.
- Four passes, six 2048 faces, eight real accumulated captures each: 192 captures. Existing bounded Cubeless quality profile used; restoration reports success. No normalized BC7 delivery or RGB clipping was introduced.
- Editor-only capture wrapper: `scripts/rx_three_basis_dome_capture.py`. It executes an isolated copy of the verified capture implementation and does not patch shared module globals.

## Shading

The material uses one cloud basis texture instead of Positive/Negative. Integrated RGB receives the existing gain of four; alpha is not multiplied by the gain. Upper/lower lighting selects the dominant lobe, with a smooth -12 to +12 degree transition rather than broad averaging. Ambient transport uses the smaller of the two beauty lobes so their bright regions do not automatically fill each other's shadows. Back response is limited by forward-view alignment and optical-thickness attenuation; it follows scattering strength and does not brighten the entire interior. Existing palette, cloud motion, shade-remap controls, shared horizon fog and celestial holdout remain.

The three fixed directions do not retain six-way lateral relighting. Existing cloud-shadow projection and independent cards retain their original resources. Thus the cloud dome uses one RGBA basis texture, not the entire scene's every texture combined into one resource.

## Validation

Materials and BP compiled with zero errors/warnings. Live CloudDome MID resolves to the new parent and HDR texture. Direct dependencies of the new material, MI, BP, map and texture contain no MCP references. Current BP values were preserved, including TimeOfDay 11.712, and the original camera was retained. Reviewed fixed-motion six-way/three-way captures and sunset/night views; restored live animation and the original time. This is an art comparison candidate, not a claim of six-way equivalence. Packaged, mobile and reflection-capture validation were not performed.

Evidence: `Saved/RXThreeBasisDome/` (parameter copy report, comparison screenshots, verification log) and `Saved/RXSkyBaking/Cubeless_Beauty45_20260920/bake.json` (capture/restore report).

## Daytime underside refinement

Added material scalar `DayUndersideStrength` (Cloud Shading, default 0.65, Korean tooltip). A continuous lower-facing mask uses R/(R+G) from the upper/lower bake, weighted by dense coverage and daylight elevation. After palette/remap/edge grading, cloud RGB is attenuated by this mask before celestial holdout compensation and final shared fog. Thus later palette lifting cannot erase all underside shading; bright upper-facing lobes, thin coverage, alpha and horizon fog remain intact. No rebake or additional texture sample is required. This is an art-directed mask, not a recovered geometric normal. The control is in the material instance, not a new BP instance variable.

Verified noon at an identical camera and frozen cloud motion: `noon_underside_off.png` versus `noon_underside_on.png` shows stronger lower/internal shade while keeping upper highlights. Returned to the user's TimeOfDay 16.832 and normal motion. Material compiled with zero errors; executable workflow full verification is recorded in `underside_full.log`. Authoring helper: `scripts/refine_rx_three_basis_underside_ue.py`.

## Twilight shadow correction

### Follow-up: actual internal silhouette cause

The subsequent daytime complaint isolated the hard internal silhouette to `DayUndersideStrength`: setting it to zero on the live MID removed the boundary without changing the bake. The R/(R+G) threshold was incorrectly treating opposing integrated transport as a geometric facing mask; occlusion also changes this ratio. The earlier palette adjustment did not fix this cause. Replaced that ratio with bounded continuous attenuation `0.38 * exp(-4 * R/max(coverage,0.04))`. Default strength remains 0.65, limiting extra darkening to 24.7% before daylight/density gates. Existing baked shade remains. No rebake was needed. Reviewed the actual reported view at time 7.680, with evidence `shape_before.png`, `shape_no_underside.png`, `shape_fixed.png`; checked dusk and restored user time/camera. Helper: `scripts/fix_rx_three_basis_shadow_mask_ue.py`; verification: `shadow_mask_full.log`.

The inherited sunset grade replaced up to 78% of cloud lighting with a palette whose shadow response was constant below transport 0.04. This could turn dense clouds into flat purple areas. The three-basis material now uses a continuous transport/(transport+0.12) response, blends the shadow tint with the local sky, and limits palette replacement to 42%. Daytime underside attenuation now fades in over solar elevation 12–30 degrees instead of 2–18 degrees, avoiding extra low-sun darkening. Coverage, celestial occlusion, fog and the bake are unchanged.

Live review used frozen-motion before/after captures at the current 6.912 time and noon, plus an evening 17.5 capture. Current camera, time 6.912 and live motion were restored; the user's already-dirty level was not saved over. Material compiled and saved with zero errors. Direct material dependency audit found only the curve atlas and baked texture, with no MCP references. Evidence: `Saved/RXThreeBasisDome/twilight_fixed_before.png`, `twilight_fixed_after.png`, `evening_center_after.png`, and `twilight_full.log`. Authoring helper: `scripts/refine_rx_three_basis_twilight_ue.py`. Fixed three-direction illumination still cannot reproduce arbitrary six-direction relighting.
